To prioritize routes based on cumulative IGP metrics for inbound traffic flows, enable the AIGP attribute on relevant BGP sessions:

```console
configure router
    bgp
        group <group_name>
            aigp
        exit
```

Alternatively, apply AIGP per neighbor:
```console
configure router
    bgp
        group <group_name>
            neighbor <ip_address>
                aigp
```

Ensure the following prerequisites are met:
- AIGP must be supported and consistently enabled across all participating routers in the path
- IGP metrics must be properly configured network-wide
- BGP sessions are established with peers advertising AIGP-enabled routes

The AIGP attribute will propagate cumulative IGP metrics, making them available for BGP path selection decisions. The router will then prefer routes with lower total IGP costs during best-path selection.
