To restrict BGP peer sessions from negotiating 4-byte ASN capabilities for backward compatibility with legacy 2-byte ASN equipment, apply the following configuration at the appropriate BGP hierarchy level (instance, group, or neighbor):

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "LEGACY_PEERS"
        disable-4byte-asn
    exit
```

Replace `"LEGACY_PEERS"` with the actual group name containing your legacy peers. For granular control per specific neighbor, use:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "LEGACY_PEERS"
        neighbor <legacy_peer_IP>
            disable-4byte-asn
        exit
    exit
```

