To achieve BGP-based load balancing with accurate bandwidth attributes during internal redistribution on your Nokia 7750 SR routers, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <ebgp_group_name>
        link-bandwidth
            accept-from-ebgp ipv4
        exit
    exit
    group <ibgp_group_name>
        link-bandwidth
            aggregate-used-paths ipv4
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
1. **`accept-from-ebgp ipv4`** (under EBGP group):  
   - Allows the router to process and store the link-bandwidth extended community received from Juniper EBGP peers for IPv4 prefixes.

2. **`aggregate-used-paths ipv4`** (under IBGP group):  
   - When re-advertising IPv4 routes via `next-hop-self` to internal peers, this command sums the bandwidth values from all active multipaths.  
   - Preserves accurate aggregated bandwidth metrics in the link-bandwidth extended community during redistribution.

**Key Notes:**  
- Replace `<ebgp_group_name>` and `<ibgp_group_name>` with your actual EBGP/Juniper and IBGP peer group names.  
- Ensure multipath BGP is enabled to utilize parallel links.  
- The aggregated bandwidth is automatically attached to routes advertised to IBGP peers, enabling downstream load balancing based on the summed bandwidth.  

This configuration maintains bandwidth integrity across internal redistribution while optimizing traffic distribution across parallel links.
