To implement stricter egress route control using extended communities on Nokia 7750 SR nodes, configure BGP Outbound Route Filtering (ORF) with automatic extended community policy generation. This ensures scalable classification and filtering based on route target attributes:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <peer-group-name>
        outbound-route-filtering
            extended-community
                send-orf
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key aspects:**
- `send-orf` enables automatic ORF policy generation using configured route targets, accepted client ORFs, and local route targets
- Filters routes dynamically based on extended community attributes
- Scales by eliminating manual policy maintenance
- Negotiates ORF capability with peers to reduce unnecessary route advertisements

Apply this configuration at the BGP group or neighbor level where stricter egress control is required. The system automatically handles policy updates when route target configurations change.
