To ensure uninterrupted IPv6 traffic forwarding during routing protocol restarts on your Nokia 7750 SR, configure BGP Graceful Restart for the IPv6 address family with these CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        enable-notification
        restart-time 300
        stale-routes-time 300
    exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `graceful-restart` globally enables BGP Graceful Restart helper functionality for all supported address families (including IPv6).  
- `enable-notification` allows session preservation during NOTIFICATION events.  
- `restart-time 300` sets the maximum restart duration advertised to peers (5 minutes).  
- `stale-routes-time 300` maintains stale IPv6 routes for 5 minutes during control plane transitions.  

> **Note:** This configuration works with default IPv6 BGP peers. For neighbor-specific tuning, apply the same parameters under `group` or `neighbor` contexts. Verify peer compatibility with `show router bgp neighbor <ip> capabilities`.
