To implement multipath advertisement and negotiation for unlabeled IPv4 prefixes on your Nokia 7750 SR routers, use the following CLI configuration commands. This enables sending up to 8 paths per prefix and receiving multiple paths from peers:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "TRANSIT_PROVIDER_GROUP"
        add-paths
            ipv4 send 8 receive
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- **`ipv4 send 8`**: Advertises up to 8 best paths per unlabeled IPv4 prefix to the peer.  
- **`receive`**: Enables negotiation to accept multiple paths per prefix from the peer.  
- Apply this under the BGP group context for your transit provider (replace `TRANSIT_PROVIDER_GROUP` with your group name).  

This configuration ensures optimal path diversity while maintaining backward compatibility—peers without Add-Paths support will automatically revert to single-path exchange.
