To implement BGP route damping for suppressing unstable prefixes while preserving stable paths, configure the following:

```cli
/configure router policy-options
begin
policy-statement "damp-flapping-routes"
    entry 10
        action accept
            damp half-life 15 reuse 750 suppress 3000 max-suppress 60
        exit
    exit
commit
exit

/configure router bgp
    group <peer-group-name>
        neighbor <peer-ip>
            import "damp-flapping-routes"
            damping
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key parameters explained:**  
- `half-life 15`: Penalty halves every 15 minutes  
- `reuse 750`: Re-advertise route when penalty falls below 750  
- `suppress 3000`: Suppress route when penalty exceeds 3000  
- `max-suppress 60`: Maximum suppression time of 60 minutes  

**Verification:**  
```cli
show router bgp routes damping
show router bgp routes <prefix> detail
```

> **Note:** Replace `<peer-group-name>` and `<peer-ip>` with your specific BGP peer details. The thresholds balance suppression effectiveness (high suppress/reuse ratio) with reconvergence time (controlled max-suppress period).
