To gracefully deactivate BGP neighbor monitoring (peer tracking) on your Nokia 7750 SRs during maintenance, use the following CLI commands:

### To disable BGP peer tracking **globally** (all neighbors):
```cli
configure router
    bgp
        no enable-peer-tracking
```

### To disable BGP peer tracking for a **specific group**:
```cli
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            no enable-peer-tracking
```

### To disable BGP peer tracking for a **specific neighbor**:
```cli
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            neighbor <neighbor-IP>
                no enable-peer-tracking
```

### Post-maintenance re-enablement:
To restore peer tracking after testing, reconfigure with `enable-peer-tracking` at the same hierarchy level.

### Key notes:
1. These commands **do not tear down BGP sessions**—existing adjacencies remain active.
2. Peer tracking is disabled immediately without impacting the control plane.
3. Default behavior (`no enable-peer-tracking`) suppresses accelerated session drops during route withdrawals, preventing false alarms during failover tests.

Choose the configuration level (global/group/neighbor) based on your targeted scope.
