## Proposed answer:
To resolve path MTU discovery issues and enable dynamic MSS adaptation for TCP sessions using ICMP feedback, configure:

```
configure router bgp
    path-mtu-discovery
exit
```

This enables the router to:
1. Set the initial TCP session MTU to the egress interface's MTU
2. Apply the DF (Don't Fragment) bit to packets
3. Dynamically adjust MTU/MSS upon receiving ICMP fragmentation-needed messages
4. Optimize throughput by automatically adapting packet sizes without manual intervention

For BGP-specific sessions, apply the command at the appropriate hierarchy (`bgp`, `group`, or `neighbor`) based on your peer scope.
