To adjust the BGP keepalive interval to 60 seconds and ensure session stability for higher-latency WAN links, configure the following commands on your Nokia 7750 SR router. These changes will reset BGP sessions, so apply them during the maintenance window:

```cli
configure router bgp
    hold-time 180
    keepalive 60
exit
```

### Key details:
1. **`keepalive 60`**: Sets the interval for BGP keepalive messages to 60 seconds (default is 30 seconds).
2. **`hold-time 180`**: Sets the hold-time to 180 seconds (3× the keepalive interval) to maintain the standard BGP timer ratio. This ensures compatibility with peers still using default settings.

### Additional stability recommendations (optional):
To minimize disruption during session resets, consider these enhancements:

```cli
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        restart-time 300
        stale-routes-time 600
    exit
    damp-peer-oscillations idle-hold-time 0 5 60 error-interval 30
exit
```

- **`restart-time 300`**: Advertises a 5-minute restart capability to peers during Graceful Restart.
- **`stale-routes-time 600`**: Preserves stale routes for 10 minutes during restarts.
- **`damp-peer-oscillations`**: Suppresses session flapping penalties using RFC 4271 recommendations.

These commands should be applied at the global BGP level. If adjustments are needed for specific groups or neighbors, use the same parameters under `group` or `neighbor` contexts.
