To set the BGP local preference to 200 for inbound route advertisements from your primary transit provider, apply the following configuration at the group or neighbor level of your Nokia 7750 SR routers. Replace `"PRIMARY-TRANSIT"` with the actual group name used for your transit provider peers.

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "PRIMARY-TRANSIT"
        local-preference 200
    exit
exit
```

**Key details:**  
- This configuration sets `local-preference 200` for all BGP routes received from peers in the specified group.  
- Higher local preference values (e.g., 200) prioritize these routes over paths with lower values (default is 100).  
- The setting persists across reloads and avoids complex policy structures by leveraging direct attribute configuration.  

If you need to apply this to specific neighbors within the group, use the neighbor-level configuration instead:
```cli
configure router bgp
    group "PRIMARY-TRANSIT"
        neighbor <neighbor_IP>
            local-preference 200
        exit
    exit
exit
```
