This configuration:
1. Marks routes with invalid origin ASes as unusable (`origin-invalid-unusable`), excluding them from best-path selection and preventing propagation to peers.
2. Prioritizes routes with valid origin validation states (`compare-origin-validation-state`), ensuring paths with verified origins are preferred during path selection.

The changes apply globally to all BGP routes, ensuring only properly validated paths are used for traffic engineering and propagation.
