To implement extended BGP graceful restart functionality on your Nokia 7750 SR router for maintaining session stability during planned maintenance, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```console
configure router
    bgp
        graceful-restart
            enable-notification
            restart-time 600
            stale-routes-time 1200
        exit
        damp-peer-oscillations idle-hold-time 5 10 30 error-interval 30
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `enable-notification`: Allows graceful session restart using BGP NOTIFICATION messages during maintenance.  
- `restart-time 600`: Extends the advertised restart timer to 600 seconds (10 minutes) for longer maintenance windows.  
- `stale-routes-time 1200`: Preserves stale routes for 1200 seconds (20 minutes), ensuring continuous forwarding during control plane interruptions.  
- `damp-peer-oscillations`: Suppresses unnecessary session re-establishment attempts with initial 5-minute hold time, exponential backoff (10 minutes → 30 minutes), and 30-minute error-free reset window.  

This configuration maintains traffic flow during control plane upgrades by extending BGP state retention beyond standard timers while minimizing peer oscillation.
