To enforce selective tunnel association for BGP-labeled unicast routes, configure the resolution filter under the labeled-routes transport tunnel family IPv4 context:

```console
/configure router bgp next-hop-resolution labeled-routes transport-tunnel
    family ipv4
        resolution filter
        resolution-filter <tunnel-type-1> [<tunnel-type-2> ...]
    exit
exit
```

**Replace `<tunnel-type-1> [<tunnel-type-2> ...]` with your specific tunnel types** from these supported options:  
`bgp`, `ldp`, `rsvp`, `sr-isis`, `sr-ospf`, `sr-policy`, `sr-te`.

**Example**: To allow only RSVP and SR-TE tunnels:  
```console
resolution-filter rsvp sr-te
```  

This configuration:
- Restricts BGP route binding exclusively to the tunnel types specified in `resolution-filter`
- Maintains full functionality for other LSP types not involved in BGP-labeled unicast resolution
- Uses `resolution filter` mode to enforce selective tunnel association while preserving standard TTM preferences among allowed types
